<title>USA: US exporters report 109,728 tonnes corn to Japan.</title>
<headline>US exporters report 109,728 tonnes corn to Japan.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department Friday said private exporters reported sales of 109,728 tonnes of corn to Japan.</p>
<p>USDA said of the total, 54,864 tonnes is for delivering during the 1996/97 marketing year and 54,864 tonnes is for delivery during the 1997/98 marketing year.</p>
<p>The marketing year for corn began Sept 1.</p>
<p>Exporters must report to USDA sales of 100,000 tonnes or more of one commodity made in one day to a single destination by 1500 ET the next business day after the sale.</p>
<p>Sales of lesser quantities must be reported weekly.</p>
<p>((Washington commodities desk, 202 898 8967))</p>
</text>
